# Goblin Engineer: "Return target artifact card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield."
# Bot1's Engineer buries Krark-Clan Ironworks (mana value 4) on turn 1. On turn 3 the only artifact card in the graveyard
# is too expensive, so the ability is not offered at all (refused). Bot1 then sacrifices a Pyrite Spellbomb (mana value 1)
# to draw a card, and now the ability is offered: it sacrifices Mox Jet and returns the Spellbomb, leaving the Ironworks
# in the graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Goblin Engineer
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mountain
Pyrite Spellbomb
Island
Island
Krark-Clan Ironworks
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Pyrite Spellbomb.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Goblin Engineer.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Search(Krark-Clan Ironworks)
? Bot1.Graveyard = Krark-Clan Ironworks
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Engineer.Activate(Ability: Return target artifact)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Pyrite Spellbomb.Activate(Ability: Draw)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Graveyard = Pyrite Spellbomb; Krark-Clan Ironworks
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Engineer.Activate(Ability: Return target artifact; Bot1.Graveyard.Pyrite Spellbomb)
Bot1.Choose(Tap Goblin Engineer)
Bot1.Choose(Mox Jet)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Mox Jet; Krark-Clan Ironworks
Bot1.Battlefield = Mountain; Mox Ruby; Goblin Engineer; Pyrite Spellbomb
